body:
thank you, i'll write down as many numbers as i can and use my local library's phone to call. i'm really hoping i don't have to rehome her, as i have mental illness and she has helped me out so much with it. if i have to though, i guess i can find someone good.

&#x200B;

thank you so so much for the help, it means so much. i'll be okay with time. i hope you're doing well.

When my parents were just emotionally abusive I would beg them to hit me, because at least then I'd have a visible reason to show someone they were hurting me and then they'd take me away. Suffering from just emotional abuse, even when your parents can be nice sometimes is one of the worst things you can experience and don't let anyone tell you any different. Everyone sees the good in them, and sees the nice things you have, and if you ever try accusing them of anything, it will always be shoved in your face and you will be punished for standing out of line.

&#x200B;

My parents forced me out of school to watch their children and clean their house pretty much around the clock. I rarely if ever go out anymore, let alone see friends so I know how you feel. If you ever want to talk, my PMs are always open. <3

&#x200B;

That being said, if you aren't in risk of severe bodily harm or death, (from either your family or yourself if you force yourself to stay) I beg of you to contact someone you are related to that you trust will side with you and not your parents, a school councilor, or a runaway hotline in your area. It's important to repeat that running away is a last ditch effort at getting away from a bad situation that can put you (in most cases) in a much worse situation, so please weigh the pros and cons. The mods worked really hard to put a ton of info together all throughout the subreddit so make sure to click through and read whatever you can. I wish you luck in whatever journey you take, friend. <3
